"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:48:59-07:00","id":673406,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/624122-techne\">Techn\u00e9 write-up</a> should probably be included somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:23:22-08:00","id":808483,"title":"","content":"Hey Dave, I wanted to ask but will there be any way to fundamentally change an object or person so that the changes &quot;stick&quot;? Basically Ontological Inertia when it comes to physical changes (Eg. turning someone into a frog) or turning one substance into another? Because, at least I'd assume, that changing back from a frog to a person is just as unbelievable as a person changing into a frog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:00:41-08:00","id":808702,"title":"","content":"Ontological Inertia tends to kick in as a secondary effect of some spells. A healing spell for instance heals, the damage removed is a permanent secondary effect.<br /> <br /> You can also render some spells permanent by giving up a point or a dot of WP to relinquish control of the spell. Which you spend is determined by how much you care about the spell remaining exactly as you left it. If you spend only a point of WP it will eventually go off message. These kinds of spells can still be dispelled though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:56:42-08:00","id":808787,"title":"","content":"It's a good question. I think I recently posted a query, where I asked, whether or not it's possible to permanently get yourself a Merit during the story by using magic, when said Merit is meant for character creation only. I gave the Ambidextrous Merit as an example. I think that sacrificing the dot of Willpower could work. I hope Dave has rules about what spells are possible to make permanent in what circumstances somewhere in the Creative Thaumaturgy section. We have the healing, after all. Why not some other spells as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:13:16-08:00","id":809423,"title":"","content":"There will be other spells, naturally. Knowing spells are an obvious example. You didn't know something, now you do and that change is permanent.<br /> <br /> Without the rules in front of me to contradict me though it seems like almost any spell could be used this way. You just make the spell do a thing (I.e. This spell gives a merit) and as long as the thing (Merit in this case) is a side effect it becomes permanent. Which I think is almost certainly not the case, though I could see a strong argument for Making spells being able to do that all the time. I","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:45:21-08:00","id":809823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=808787#post808787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good question. I think I recently posted a query, where I asked, whether or not it's possible to permanently get yourself a Merit during the story by using magic, when said Merit is meant for character creation only. I gave the Ambidextrous Merit as an example. I think that sacrificing the dot of Willpower could work. I hope Dave has rules about what spells are possible to make permanent in what circumstances somewhere in the Creative Thaumaturgy section. We have the healing, after all. Why not some other spells as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm big on shapechanging, but I find it weird that if you turn into say... a dog, anyone looking at you seems to unravel the spell, even if you're an absolutely ordinary dog. Furthermore, you'd think that it'd violate disbelief <b>more</b> to have a dog change into a person. Could be interesting if disbelief could get someone stuck in an altered form.<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance if you were to turn into something obviously supernatural, it might be obviously supernatural in origin, but the disbelief might be even worse if you changed from something obviously supernatural into something even more mundane. So if you were say, captured, in this altered state because you're a talking dog or some-such, you can't change back because to undo the transformation would invoke disbelief and paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-15-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:33:47-08:00","id":809845,"title":"","content":"To summarize my thoughts, I would say that I would allow Lasting effects to happen to things like Merits, body changes and the like, if the player payed the appropriate XP, used up a Willpower dot <i>and</i> at the same time the spell caused effects, that could at least theoretically exist in the physical world on their own. The XP would symbolize the effort the character spent on figuring out how to make effects of the spell its indirect consequences.<br /> <br /> For example, if you use magic to create a force that starts to push a bucket out of the window, and end the spell, the bucket ceases to be pushed (direct result of the spell ends), but it still falls down due to gravity, if moved far enough (indirect effect). Or, you could use a spell to manipulate gene modifying systems with absolute precision (direct effect that stops once the spell ends) to move around genes in the genome (indirect effect - the genes were basically moved by a bunch of material molecules from their own &quot;perspective&quot;, not directly created/destroyed/changed by the spell =&gt; the changes won't end once the spell does).<br /> <br /> So, you could create a fire breathing lizard as a lasting effect, if you created some kind of gas bags in his body with flammable content that would ignite after contact with air. On the other end creating a lizard that just literally makes up fire from thin air when it opens its mouth would not would not be possible on its own in material world and would continually need a support of a spell to continue to exist. This would be at best an indefinite effect that could be affected and unraveled by dissonance or be dispelled.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: This made me think about the use of these rules in Rotes. A master creates a rote that allows you to create a Lasting effect in something and then is willing to sell the rote to others who do not possess the knowledge of how to cast that kind of spell on their own. The XP cost for the effects would probably still be there (as to not break the game, same as for when the mage figures it all out on their own) - the mage in question who possesses the Rote would probably not sell it cheap, and it would increase the importance of Rotes and add another facet to the Awakened economy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 01-15-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:04:30-08:00","id":809932,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I am pretty sure the rules for permanent changes will be handled in 2e, so it's just a matter of waiting and we'll see. I think that from what we saw in previous spoilers the rules are probably going to look something like this:\u200b<br /> <br /> 1. Spend a willpower dot and have at least X successes (probably 5 for dramatic success, 3 if praxis).<br /> <br /> 2. You have your lasting stuff yay!<br /> <br /> 3. If you don't spend XP, Storyteller may still take it away for story reasons.<br /> <br /> 4. If you spend the XP, sanctity of merits applies and if the ST takes it away you get your XP back, maybe willpower too?<br /> <br /> 5. If stuff looks supernatural it still causes Dissonance. See points 3 and 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T18:08:36-08:00","id":809972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=809823#post809823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm big on shapechanging, but I find it weird that if you turn into say... a dog, anyone looking at you seems to unravel the spell, even if you're an absolutely ordinary dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. In 1e and as best I can tell from what's been released about 2e, disbelief only affects the spell if the sleeper notices the magic. The only exception to this was some ancient Atlantean things that were held together basically just by cobwebs and would tend to fall apart if a Sleeper sneezed nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:24:42-08:00","id":810045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=809932#post809932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, I am pretty sure the rules for permanent changes will be handled in 2e, so it's just a matter of waiting and we'll see. I think that from what we saw in previous spoilers the rules are probably going to look something like this:\u200b<br /> <br /> 1. Spend a willpower dot and have at least X successes (probably 5 for dramatic success, 3 if praxis).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you have a source for 1? I haven't seen anything like that. From what I recall spells are pass/fail on 1 success regardless of how long you want it to last. Exceptional successes grant extra benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T20:33:39-08:00","id":810049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=809972#post809972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't. In 1e and as best I can tell from what's been released about 2e, disbelief only affects the spell if the sleeper notices the magic. The only exception to this was some ancient Atlantean things that were held together basically just by cobwebs and would tend to fall apart if a Sleeper sneezed nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just wondering if Disbelief can maintain a spell, because it just disappearing is more unbelievable than the object's existence in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T21:23:41-08:00","id":810077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=810049#post810049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just wondering if Disbelief can maintain a spell, because it just disappearing is more unbelievable than the object's existence in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disbelief has nothing to do with belief, which is part of why it's been renamed to Dissonance in 2e, as covered in the &quot;I'll Lie To You&quot; blog entry.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, this\u2026 isn't really a general-questions sticky. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition\">We've got another thread for that</a> so you don't have to space out other people's attempts at consolidating links to threads and blog posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T22:33:26-08:00","id":810089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs?p=810077#post810077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Disbelief has nothing to do with belief, which is part of why it's been renamed to Dissonance in 2e, as covered in the &quot;I'll Lie To You&quot; blog entry.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, this\u2026 isn't really a general-questions sticky. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition\">We've got another thread for that</a> so you don't have to space out other people's attempts at consolidating links to threads and blog posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought this was a discussion thread, more or less. Doesn't seem like the place for asking in a Q&amp;A thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T04:05:19-08:00","id":810167,"title":"","content":"No, this is not a discussion thread. This was a place to keep links to spoilers for the benefit of people coming to Mage part-way through Open Development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T16:21:58-08:00","id":814521,"title":"","content":"I can lock the thread if you think that would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">On